---
description: Essential FastAPI architecture for almost every backend change
globs: backend/**/*.py
alwaysApply: true
---

Flow: Router → Service → Repository → Infrastructure/Database.

Routers stay thin: request parsing, auth dependencies, status codes, and
calling a service. No business rules, queries, external API calls, or AI
provider calls in routers.

Each `app/modules/<name>/` capability uses `models.py`, `schemas.py`,
`repository.py`, `service.py`, `router.py`. Services call repositories.
Query logic stays out of `service.py`. Business workflows stay out of
`repository.py`.

A module may import `app/core/` and its own files only. Cross-module work
goes through an explicit public service or contract. No circular imports.
`backend/tool/verify_architecture.py` enforces this.

Raise domain exceptions from `app/core/exceptions.py` in services. Map them
at the HTTP boundary to `{"code", "message", "details"}`. Do not return
stack traces, ORM errors, provider errors, or secrets.

Pydantic schemas are the API contract. Do not return SQLAlchemy models.
Validate external input. Business rules that depend on application state
belong in the service.

Configuration comes from the project settings. Never hardcode secrets, API
keys, passwords, tokens, or credentials.

Before adding a helper, search for an existing one. Reuse the same
responsibility. Do not add `utils.py`, `helpers.py`, `common.py`,
`manager.py`, or `base_service.py` without a clear shared owner.

Inspect the current module first. Follow existing patterns. Make the
smallest correct change. Do not refactor unrelated code or add a dependency
unless the task needs it. Do not scaffold new modules unless asked.
